  "prefLabel": "Puc 402.14 Payphone service provider (PSP)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 402.14 \"Payphone service provider (PSP)\" means a person or entity that offers telephone service on a fee per call basis with payment due at the time of the call, and that has been issued a certificate of registration by the commission to provide payphone service.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note # 1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Puc 400) #14029, eff 7-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc400.html"
